id: pm-csv-bwrv
title: Apply edited spreadsheet exports without overwriting concurrent tracker changes
description: Export an explicit item/revision/field-digest edit session and import the edited table as a three-way patch. Reuse keyed identity and existing atomic compensation; this is distinct from the general terminal keyed retry defect and does not replace the SDK transaction coordinator.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: added,concurrency,csv
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:06:53.134Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T15:30:58.025Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T15:30:56.521Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T15:30:56.521Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Two editors on one exported table cannot overwrite newer tracker values; terminal keyed updates stay idempotent; a stale digest causes zero item/history writes; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON receipts and actionable refusals; documented example and real public-tracker copy validation without git; targeted regression revert proof and unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates
unblock_note: Owner requested proceeding with the package callback deadline mitigation; retain upstream atomic persistence fencing as an open follow-up in pm-cli issue 1549.
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:07:08.204Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against current CLI source and fleet sibling documentation: native bulk keyed upsert and workspace transactions already exist; pm-csv keyed identity, atomic coordinator integration and full-document compensation are reused. pm-ado has remote revision-checked three-way sync specific to Azure. pm-beads, pm-todos, pm-jira and pm-linear have format/service round trips, without a spreadsheet edit-session contract. No matching CSV session item found by context/search/open inventory. pm-csv-0rvm remains the separate legacy terminal retry bug. Reconciliation PR 178 closes unrelated delivered items; none will be edited. Registry latest CLI is 2026.10.21; repository pin remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T20:13:38.356Z",codex-agent,"Implemented versioned CSV plus baseline session JSON, explicit stable item/history/field digests, bounded typed refusals, three-way scalar patches and per-item locked conflict checks. Uses the existing SDK coordinator plus CSV full-document compensation. Ten targeted real non-git tracker scenarios pass, including two editors, zero-write stale preflight, terminal identity/lifecycle preservation, convergent retry, native-writer races and interrupted resume. Status is intentionally read-only with a lifecycle-command remedy; editable fields and boundaries are documented. Host canonicalization trims trailing body whitespace, now normalized before comparison to preserve retry idempotency."
  "2026-10-21T20:17:51.616Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation passed on a non-git scratch copy of public pm-csv main 1f7e523b6d5539264d3316362665506486eeea3a: 118 real items, zero enumeration warnings, 17 columns/6 editable fields; session JSON 114257 bytes and CSV 97461 bytes. Three rows across open/in-progress/terminal states applied; one concurrent unedited field survived. Retry applied zero. Four whole-corpus raw-document/history hash comparisons proved zero writes for unchanged import, retry, second-editor conflict and altered revision. Actual built CLI exported 118 items with no git executable. Full-table JSON/TOON receipts measured 89/61 bytes. Single sample took 31.32 seconds. Details: docs/spreadsheet-validation.md."
  "2026-10-21T20:18:51.013Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only conflicts() with an empty conflict list, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"two editors|native writer after preflight\" test/roundtrip.test.ts. Both selected regressions failed (0 pass, 2 fail, exit 1) because expected conflict refusals disappeared. Restored the function byte-for-byte. With the guard restored the targeted suite passes 12/12, and roundtrip.ts measures 100% lines, 100% branches and 100% functions under targeted V8 coverage. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication checks pass. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-21T20:20:54.652Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted suite now passes 13/13 through the PM-linked runner. Added a native-convergence receipt regression: applied counts only rows actually mutated during this attempt, including zero when a native writer supplies the desired value after preflight. Local typecheck/test-typecheck/lint/docstring/duplication checks pass. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so the linked runner printed success without persisting a run record; this comment records its 13 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip result. No tracker policy was changed."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:19.136Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39669745243 passed on implementation head 5a7d03c526ee7081e2dea78601063f40d39affb2: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 300/300 tests on Node 22 and Node 26, with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. All four gate executions report four required source files and 100% lines/branches/functions at unchanged thresholds; packed npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum scenarios pass. CI strict tracker health passes. This is script-runner/Bun-launcher evidence, not a forced native-Bun claim for every test."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:23.737Z",codex-agent,"Final review cleanup replaces an array used only for its length with a numeric row counter (DeepScan USELESS_ARRAY). The SDK also refuses non-array/non-string table input as csv_edit_invalid and clones the validated baseline to prevent caller alias mutation. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass; affected receipt/recovery checks pass 3/3, malformed-input checks pass 2/2. A final-head CI rerun will verify the resulting commit. Review availability is separate: CodeRabbit skipped automatic review, Sourcery reported quota exhaustion, Greptile reported an expired trial, and cubic skipped. No bot was mentioned or manually triggered."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:27.633Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and evidence are ready for orchestrator verification in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/179. Releasing the implementation claim; the item remains in progress and must not be closed by this agent. Final-head CI status and run counts will be recorded in the PR after the cleanup commit passes. Limits: status is read-only; hosted Postgres/MCP acceptance is unmeasured; late transaction failures require reconciliation when guarded compensation cannot safely restore."
  "2026-10-21T22:14:10.766Z",codex-agent,"PR 179 review round: verified both unresolved threads against the remote head. Fix formula-leading editable cells with a symmetric display codec and retain transaction causes plus nested item/field conflicts. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Self-review the full PR for the same classes. Use targeted regressions with behavioral revert proofs, typecheck and lint locally; unchanged full npm and Bun release gates run in CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:18:13.527Z",codex-agent,"Verified PR 179 threads PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6u-OsL and PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6u-OsN. Editable checkout cells now escape all six formula triggers and literal leading apostrophes; apply decodes recognized prefixes before baseline comparison while preserving raw sidecars and digests. Transaction refusals retain the original cause and conflicts across shared/cyclic cause and AggregateError graphs, including a real concurrent-writer compensation refusal. Full-diff self-review also fixed dropped causes in snapshot reads and checkout/apply IO adapters. Regression tests use real non-git trackers; no SDK mocks. The latest CodeRabbit review contains no outside-diff or nitpick findings."
  "2026-10-21T22:18:15.992Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (each variant restored byte-for-byte afterward): toCell identity: 0 pass/1 fail; fromCell identity: 0/1; findConflicts returning an empty list: 0/2; restoring the lossy transaction catch: 0/4; removing snapshot cause retention: 0/1; removing command IO cause retention: 0/1. Every invocation exited 1. Commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"spreadsheet display\" test/roundtrip.test.ts (encode and decode separately); patterns \"transaction failures|transaction diagnostics\" (collector), \"native writer after preflight|interrupted transaction|transaction failures|transaction diagnostics\" (catch), \"missing and history-drifted\" (snapshot), and \"command checkout/apply\" (IO). Restored encode/decode and nested-graph regressions passed 2/2 before the revert runs; final linked suite follows."
  "2026-10-21T22:19:13.426Z",codex-agent,"Final restored PM-linked npm exec -- node --test test/roundtrip.test.ts passed 16/16 tests with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todo. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint and git diff --check pass. Existing test-result-tracking policy is disabled, so the CLI returned reported_tests success without persisting a run record; this comment records the counts. No local timeout occurred. dist is generated and ignored, with no committed dist files to update. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will be verified on the pushed head in CI and linked from the PR body. Review claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-22T11:14:35.934Z",codex-agent,"PR 179 review round: pulled the remote head and merged current origin/main first. Verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vA7R4: quoted multiline LF-to-CRLF conversion creates false edits and conflicts. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. Normalize newline-only differences across every editable field while retaining exact baseline bytes; also cover CRLF baselines saved as LF. Genuine content edits retain normal conflict protection. Full npm and Bun release gates will run at unchanged thresholds; no review threads will be replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-22T11:19:32.323Z",codex-agent,"Verified fix for PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vA7R4 and self-reviewed every editable-field comparison in the whole PR. All six fields use baseline-preserving LF/CRLF equivalence; regressions cover multiline title/body/assignee/sprint/release, LF and CRLF baselines, concurrent unedited body changes, dry-run zero writes, genuine edited-body conflicts, application and retry. Targeted node --test --test-name-pattern=\"newline-only|CRLF conversion\" test/roundtrip.test.ts passed 2/2. Behavioral revert proof: restored only plans() from the pre-fix commit, then node --test --test-name-pattern=newline-only test/roundtrip.test.ts failed 0 pass/1 fail (exit 1, false changed count 1 instead of 0). Restored the fixed function byte-for-byte. npm ci passed (zero vulnerabilities); isolated pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passed all 10 checks with no integrity/history drift. Default global-extension skew is pre-existing and isolated from repository acceptance. The initial PM-linked run hit its 120-second runner timeout after 12 passing cases under shared-host load; retry uses --timeout 600, with assertions and release thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T11:23:28.221Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-linked suite passed 18/18 tests with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo using pm test pm-csv-bwrv --run --progress --timeout 600. Elapsed 244 seconds under host load; the initial 120-second timeout was infrastructure-only and passed on retry. Existing test-result persistence is disabled, so these counts are recorded here. Generated dist was rebuilt and is ignored; no committed dist paths exist. Full npm and Bun release gates follow on the same code and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T11:31:33.732Z",codex-agent,"Local isolated npm release gate passed typecheck, workflow validation, build, lint, duplication and docstrings (99 declarations in 12 files). Stopped that local gate during coverage because shared-host saturation made existing recovery cases take 90-100 seconds each; no assertion failure had been reported. This is not a full local gate pass. The full unchanged npm run release:check and bun run release:check will be verified on the pushed head in CI, including both Node versions, before work starts on PR 178. The separate linked suite passed 18/18 on retry; exact revert proof is recorded above."
  "2026-10-22T13:42:48.001Z",codex-agent,"New review round on unchanged remote head e7c656a; worktree clean and current origin/main remains an ancestor. Fetched both unresolved threads with all comments and complete pagination; latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vNO6Q is a valid README command-name error: use Apply rather than Import. PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vNO6H targets host SDK mutateItem write fencing: installed pinned 2026.10.15 acquireLock uses TTL-based stale takeover, while mutateItemWithDeferredHistoryContext writes after the asynchronous callback without a lease-ownership/revision fence. Verify with a real non-git scratch tracker. The queue rules explicitly forbid work in upstream pm-cli; no dependency patch or SDK pin bump is authorized. Record an evidence-backed host blocker rather than claiming a package-level check fixes the write race. Self-review the whole PR for claims of unconditional conflict protection."
  "2026-10-22T13:46:27.031Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed host blocker PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vNO6H with node --test test/repros/sdk-lease-overrun.ts: 0 pass/1 fail, exit 1. No SDK/clock/lock-file mock: a real one-second lease expired while the first callback awaited; a second native mutateItem committed, then the stale writer committed over it with no refusal. Receipt: takeoverCompleted=true, staleWriterRefused=false, newerValuePreserved=false. Follow-up pm-csv-sdk-write-fence records the required host fix. Upstream edits remain forbidden by queue rules, so this valid thread remains an explicit unresolved blocker; documentation changes are not presented as remediation. Full-PR self-review also found an unconditional prevented-overwrites claim in the transaction error remedy; correct it and its regression alongside the README Apply/Import wording and lease-boundary documentation."
  "2026-10-22T13:48:29.158Z",codex-agent,"Regression proofs completed and restored byte-for-byte: reverting only the README Apply word to Import makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"spreadsheet comparison\" test/packaging.test.ts fail 0 pass/1 fail, exit 1. Restoring only applyEditSession() from the pre-round commit makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"transaction failures retain\" test/roundtrip.test.ts fail 0 pass/1 fail, exit 1, because the error remedy again overclaims prevented overwrites. Both restored targeted tests pass 1/1 each. PM-linked pm test pm-csv-bwrv --run --progress --timeout 600 passes both commands: roundtrip 18/18 and packaging 8/8, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. npm run build and npm run build:test pass; dist is ignored and has no committed paths. Existing test-result persistence remains disabled; counts are recorded here. The separate SDK lease-overrun assertion remains red 0/1 and is explicitly documented as blocker evidence outside the normal release suite, not a passing regression or a fix. No SDK/pin change was made. Full npm/Bun gates at unchanged thresholds follow."
  "2026-10-22T13:53:46.660Z",codex-agent,"The local isolated npm release gate passed typecheck, release-workflow validation, build, lint, duplication and docstrings (99 declarations / 12 files). Stopped it during coverage as shared-host recovery cases slowed to roughly 20 seconds each; no assertion failure was reported, and this partial run is not counted as a complete pass. Verify the full unchanged npm and Bun release gates on the pushed head in CI. Package tests remain distinct from the known failing standalone host-SDK safety assertion. The feature remains in progress with blocker pm-csv-sdk-write-fence; no upstream code, dependency pin, threshold, thread state, merge or release was changed."
  "2026-10-22T15:47:51.413Z",codex-agent,"New round at clean remote head b08e5a7; main is already an ancestor. Read both unresolved threads and all comments with complete pagination; latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings. Owner authorizes a package callback deadline guard: record a monotonic callback start and effective locks.ttl_seconds, then refuse before callback return at TTL minus a safety margin. Apply the shared guard to forward edits and compensation callbacks, turn the existing lease-overrun repro into passing release-suite coverage, and prove failure with the guard/wiring reverted. Keep the scope honest: this bounds callback duration, while atomic fencing at the later SDK persistence boundary remains upstream in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1549. Also fix PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vQulv: byte/hash equality demonstrates unchanged content, not absence of physical writes. No upstream source or pin changes are needed."
  "2026-10-22T15:59:26.155Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the owner-authorized monotonic callback deadline for both native mutateItem callbacks (forward apply and compensation), including no-op returns, using effective locks.ttl_seconds minus ten percent capped at one second. Exhaustion throws typed csv_lease_expired with re-run remedy. Self-review extended the same budget to checkout/prior snapshots and representation restoration, and removed an unconditional compensation docstring claim. Extracted shared EditRefusal without changing public exports. Real non-git lease suite passed 8/8, including SDK and separate CLI takeover writers, applyPlan wiring, both compensation phases and inclusive margin boundaries. Revert proofs, with only the named implementation restored then fixed bytes restored: guardEditMutation -> 0/2 (both newer values overwritten); applyPlan -> 0/1 (missing refusal); compensateUpdate -> 0/2; snapshot -> 0/1; captureUpdateCompensation -> 0/1. Every reverted command exited 1. Commands: node --test test/repros/sdk-lease-overrun.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"applyPlan refuses\" test/lease-guard.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"compensation (callback|representation)\" test/lease-guard.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"checkout refuses\" test/lease-guard.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"capture refuses\" test/lease-guard.test.ts. PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6vQulv: corrected evidence wording to zero content changes, explicitly noting invisible identical-content writes; restoring only that document makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"public tracker hashes\" test/packaging.test.ts fail 0/1, exit 1. Earlier historical zero-write descriptions based on byte/hash comparisons should be read as unchanged-content evidence. The callback budget mitigates overrun; atomic persistence fencing remains upstream in pm-cli issue 1549, including delays before callback entry or after return. Dependency pin unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T16:00:17.905Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-linked suite passed all three commands: roundtrip 18/18, packaging 9/9 and lease guard 8/8, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Runner used --timeout 600; no timeout occurred this round. Existing result persistence is disabled, so counts are recorded here. Build, test build, lint, duplication, docstrings and diff whitespace checks passed. Regenerated dist is ignored and no committed dist files exist. Full isolated npm/Bun release gates now run at unchanged 100 percent lines/branches/functions, including the two new production modules; exact pushed-head CI will also be checked."
  "2026-10-22T16:12:03.812Z",codex-agent,"Full local release gates passed: isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 315/315 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, with 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all six configured source files at unchanged thresholds. Environment: fresh temporary HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Both complete gates passed typecheck, workflow contract, build, lint, zero duplication, docstrings (93 declarations / 14 files), production audit, packing, npm-current/Bun-current/npm-minimum packed acceptance, changelog and publish/date verification. No timeout or retry this round. PM-linked SDK follow-up repro passed 2/2. Isolated strict health accepts all 10 checks with zero integrity/history drift failures (existing telemetry-queue and stale-item advisories remain). Added-content privacy scan passes and both existing history byte prefixes are preserved. Main and remote PR head remain unchanged. Release claims for orchestrator verification, commit append-only PM evidence with the code, then verify exact pushed-head CI and record its URL/counts in the PR body; items remain in progress."
  "2026-10-23T15:30:39.216Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERED: merged PR #179 (d5dbdb0a52e3e25ee79d95b98cf0b7585cd5602d) is an ancestor of audited main cca10876ae5a4fcb505ffe533e00211941659ecc. Inspected on main: test/roundtrip.test.ts, docs/spreadsheet-validation.md. Two-editor/stale-digest checks refuse before item/history/journal writes; terminal keyed retries are idempotent and concurrent untouched values survive. Typed gitless SDK/CLI, public-copy, revert and unchanged full npm/Bun gates are retained. This tracker audit inspected existing tests/files; it does not claim a new full product test run."
